B.bAm=new A.m1(B.afM,B.a9m,"Snapshots \u2014 What, Why, When","A snapshot is a frozen copy of a month's totals saved to Firestore.\n\nWhy: Rather than re-querying all past bills on every load, the snapshot captures final totals once and reads them instantly.\n\nWhen to save: Only after a month is fully closed. Cannot snapshot the current month.\n\nStaleness: If you add a transaction dated inside an already-snapshotted month, it becomes stale (\u26a0). Recreate it to include the new data.\n\nSchema: Amounts are stored by GST rate slab dynamically (byRate map), so all future rate additions are supported automatically.")
B.aas=new A.F(1,0.054901960784313725,0.4549019607843137,0.5647058823529412,B.A)
B.bAq=new A.m1(B.J6,B.aas,"How Net GST Payable is Calculated","Net GST Payable = Output GST (Sales) \u2212 Input GST (Purchases / ITC)\n\nComponent-wise:\n\u2022 Net IGST = Sales IGST \u2212 Purchase IGST\n\u2022 Net CGST = Sales CGST \u2212 Purchase CGST\n\u2022 Net SGST = Sales SGST \u2212 Purchase SGST\n\nNegative means ITC > output tax for that slab \u2014 the excess can offset other components per GST rules.\n\nSummary card = period only. GST Reconciliation Combined row adds the opening carry-fwd for the full picture.")
